</section>
<section>


<h2>
What Is Wordle?
</h2>


<p>

Wordle is a daily word puzzle where players try to discover one hidden five-letter word within six attempts.

The game became popular because it combines simple rules with strategic thinking. Every guess provides information that helps narrow down the possible answer.

</p>


<p>

Instead of randomly guessing, successful players use letter patterns, common words, and previous feedback to make smarter choices.

</p>


</section>







<section>


<h2>
How Does Wordle Work?
</h2>


<p>

Each day, Wordle provides a new five-letter challenge. Players enter a word and receive feedback after every attempt.

The goal is to identify the correct answer before using all six guesses.

</p>



<h3>
Step 1: Enter A Five-Letter Word
</h3>


<p>

Your first guess should contain useful letters. Many players choose words with common vowels and frequently used consonants.

</p>




<h3>
Step 2: Analyze The Colored Tiles
</h3>


<p>

After submitting a guess, Wordle shows colored tiles that reveal information about the hidden word.

Use these clues to improve your next attempt.

</p>


</section>







<section>


<h2>
Understanding Wordle Colors
</h2>




<div class="tiles">



<div>

<span class="green">
A
</span>


<p>
Green means the letter is correct and placed in the correct position.
</p>


</div>




<div>


<span class="yellow">
B
</span>


<p>
Yellow means the letter exists in the answer but is in the wrong position.
</p>


</div>




<div>


<span class="gray">
C
</span>


<p>
Gray means the letter does not appear in the answer.
</p>


</div>



</div>


</section>








<section>


<h2>
Wordle Rules Explained
</h2>


<ul>


<li>
You get six attempts to solve the puzzle.
</li>


<li>
Your guess must contain exactly five letters.
</li>


<li>
Each guess provides clues about the answer.
</li>


<li>
Some answers may contain repeated letters.
</li>


<li>
A new puzzle appears every day.
</li>


</ul>



</section>








<section>


<h2>
How Many Guesses Do You Get In Wordle?
</h2>


<p>

Every Wordle puzzle gives players six attempts to find the correct five-letter answer.

The challenge is not only finding the word but also using each guess efficiently.

</p>


<p>

Strong players use early guesses to discover important letters rather than only trying to solve immediately.

</p>


</section>








<section>


<h2>
Best Beginner Wordle Strategies
</h2>




<h3>
1. Choose A Strong Starting Word
</h3>


<p>

A good opening word contains common letters and multiple vowels. This helps reveal useful information quickly.

Many players prefer words containing letters like A, E, R, S, T, L, and N.

</p>





<h3>
2. Avoid Repeating Incorrect Letters
</h3>


<p>

If Wordle marks a letter as gray, avoid using it again unless you are testing a specific possibility.

</p>





<h3>
3. Use Information, Not Random Guesses
</h3>


<p>

Every guess should help you learn something new. Consider possible letter positions before submitting another word.

</p>



</section>







<section>


<h2>
Common Wordle Mistakes Beginners Make
</h2>


<ul>


<li>

Using difficult words with uncommon letters too early.

</li>


<li>

Ignoring yellow letters.

</li>


<li>

Repeating eliminated letters.

</li>


<li>

Guessing without considering previous clues.

</li>


<li>

Revealing the answer too quickly instead of using hints.

</li>


</ul>



</section>







